  urldate = {2024-12-10},
  abstract = {The intent of this chapter is to provide an overview of the topic as well as the scope, structure, and contents of the book. First, we describe the meaning of the terms in the book title: forest landscape, disturbance, and simulation modeling, based on a brief review of the literature. While not a critical review of terminology and proposal of a suite of new terms, we anticipate these clarifications will help reader comprehend the scope of the discussions in the 10 subsequent chapters. We also ensure to retain familiarity with commonly used terms in landscape ecology parlance. The forest landscape disturbance is viewed in toto, as a process that includes causal factors, state of forest landscape when disturbed, the perturbed state after the disturbance, and the progression of recovery from the disruption. The anatomy of forest landscape disturbance models, in the two commonly used categories of mechanistic and empirical, is reviewed briefly in relation to the disturbance process. Second, we outline the overall structure and sequence of the subsequent chapters to guide the reader.},
